<title>NETHERLANDS: Ahold seals Brazilian takeover.</title>
<headline>Ahold seals Brazilian takeover.</headline>
<text>
<p>ZAANDAM, Netherlands, Dec 20 - Dutch retailer Koninklijke Ahold NV said on Friday it had reached a full agreement on buying a 50 percent stake in Brazilian retail group Bompreco.</p>
<p>&quot;After establishing Bompreco's balance sheet as on December 31, 1996, the final acquisition price will be set,&quot; the Dutch group said in a statement. No further details were given.</p>
<p>Ahold said in November it wanted to buy 50 percent of Bompreco, which is Brazil's fourth largest food retailer with 1995 sales of about $1.4 billion.</p>
